  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA weak trough moves through the Ohio Valley today. Conditions remain \ndry and mild with highs in the middle to upper 60s. Southerly flow \nand clouds increase on tonight into Wednesday ahead of an \napproaching low pressure system. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA low pressure system moves through the area on Wednesday \nnight/Thursday morning. Showers are likely to occur in the warm \nsector ahead of the low. Much colder air advects in behind the low \non Thursday afternoon leading to temperatures dropping or holding \nsteady in the 40s all day. Some rain showers may persist through the \nday. Northwesterly winds may gust upwards of 25mph during the\nafternoon.\n\nChilly, showery, and windy conditions continue Thursday night into \nFriday as upper level shortwave troughs move through the Ohio \nValley. A few wet snowflakes are possible, although thermal profiles \nlook most likely to support rain. Precipitation chances decrease on \nSaturday while cold, northerly flow persists. Temperatures begin \nmoderating on Sunday into early next week.",
